<title>GERMANY: German 8-mo vehicle output +3 pct, exports +5 pct.</title>
<headline>German 8-mo vehicle output +3 pct, exports +5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German motor vehicle production rose by three percent in the first eight months of 1996, the German Automobile Industry Association VDA said on Tuesday. Exports rose by five percent in the period, the VDA said. It provided the following data.</p>
<p>PRODUCTION</p>
<p>				    Jan-Aug 96     Change vs Jan/Aug 95</p>
<p>    Passenger vehicles/vans 2,985,400	    +3 pct</p>
<p>    Trucks up to 6 tonnes   121,800		+4 pct</p>
<p>    Heavy trucks		73,700		 -13 pct</p>
<p>    All vehicles		3,180,800	    +3 pct</p>
<p>EXPORTS</p>
<p>				    Jan-Aug 96     Change vs Jan/Aug 95</p>
<p>    Passenger vehicles/vans 1,697,500	 +4 pct</p>
<p>    Trucks up to 6 tonnes   79,600	    +18 pct</p>
<p>    Heavy trucks		44,500	    -8 pct</p>
<p>    All vehicles		1,821,600	 + 5 pct</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
